ible PDFs."}, {"v": "accommodation:AssistiveTechnology", "n": "Assistive Technology", "d": "Assistive technology and software to enable or improve access.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:AssistiveTechnology\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:AudioCaptioning", "n": "Audio Captioning", "d": "Displays for text corresponding to spoken words and audio cues.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:AudioCaptioning\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:CaptioningAndTranscripts", "n": "Captioning and Transcripts", "d": "Captioning and/or transcripts for audio and video content.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:CaptioningAndTranscripts\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:ClearSignage", "n": "Clear Signage", "d": "Clear and simple signage with high contrast and easy-to-read fonts.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:ClearSignage\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:ColorBlindness", "n": "Color Blindness", "d": "Accessibility feature or accommodation that is designed to address color vision deficiency or color blindness.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:ColorBlindness\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation\ndct:description: This service typically involves adjusting the colors used in visual materials, such as websites, videos, or other digital content, to make them more distinguishable."}, {"v": "accommodation:Communication", "n": "Communication", "d": "Verbal or non-verbal communication assistance.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:Communication\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation\ndct:description: Examples include written communication, picture communication, or communication boards, telephone relay, assistive listening devices, Braille print, audio communication, or other accommodations."}, {"v": "accommodation:DietaryAccommodation", "n": "Dietary Accommodation", "d": "Alternative meal options to suit dietary needs, restrictions, or preferences.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:DietaryAccommodation\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:FacilityAccommodation", "n": "Facility Accommodation", "d": "Features, modifications or adjustments made to a physical space or facility to ensure that individuals with disabilities can access and use the space on an equal basis with others.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation\ndct:description: This can include existing features and modifications to the built environment, such as the installation of ramps, accessible restrooms, or wider doorways, as well as adjustments to lighting, signage, and other environmental factors."}, {"v": "accommodation:FlexibleSchedule", "n": "Flexible Schedule", "d": "Accommodations made for the time frames to complete work or tasks.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:FlexibleSchedule\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation\ndct:description: Examples include adjustments to working hours, extended deadlines, assessment times, or other modifications to schedules."}, {"v": "accommodation:HearingLoops", "n": "Hearing Loops", "d": "Audio induction loops that transmit signals to hearing aids, cochlear implants or other listening devices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:HearingLoops\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:MultipleLanguage", "n": "Multiple Language", "d": "Provision of materials or communication in languages other than the primary language used.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:MultipleLanguage\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:PhysicalAccessibility", "n": "Physical Accessibility", "d": "Accommodations to ensure entry and mobility throughout a facility.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:PhysicalAccessibility\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation\ndct:description: Examples include ramps or lifts for wheelchair accessibility, elevators, automatic doors, and wider doorways to accommodate mobility devices."}, {"v": "accommodation:PlainLanguage", "n": "Plain Language", "d": "Communication that is clear, concise, and easy to understand for all participants.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:PlainLanguage\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation\ndct:description: Examples include using everyday language, avoiding technical jargon, and providing relevant context to aid comprehension."}, {"v": "accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation", "n": "Resource and Service Accommodation", "d": "Accommodations that are designed to provide equal access to resources and services and are not related to physical facilities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:ScreenReader", "n": "Screen Reader", "d": "Screen reader compatibility for digital materials.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:ScreenReader\nbroader: accommodation:ResourceAndServiceAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:Sensory", "n": "Sensory", "d": "Accommodations for hypersensitivity or aversion to certain sounds, lights, textures, or smells.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:Sensory\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation\ndct:description: This can include quiet rooms, and reduced lighting."}, {"v": "accommodation:ServiceAnimal", "n": "Service Animal", "d": "Service animal accommodations, including clear guidelines, policies, and facilities for allowing service and support animals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:ServiceAnimal\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation"}, {"v": "accommodation:TactileSignage", "n": "Tactile Signage", "d": "Braille signage and tactile cues.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: accommodation:TactileSignage\nbroader: accommodation:FacilityAccommodation"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ActionStatus', 'Types of current status of an action.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ActionStatus
dct:description: Available statuses include ActiveActionStatus, CompletedActionStatus, FailedActionStatus, PotentialActionStatus.', $j$[{"v": "actionStat:ActiveActionStatus", "n": "Active Action Status", "d": "Action that is ongoing.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: actionStat:ActiveActionStatus\ndct:description: Examples include: while watching the movie, or driving to a location"}, {"v": "actionStat:CompletedActionStatus", "n": "Completed Action Status", "d": "Action that has already taken place.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: actionStat:CompletedActionStatus"}, {"v": "actionStat:FailedActionStatus", "n": "Failed Action Status", "d": "Action that failed to complete.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: actionStat:FailedActionStatus\ndct:description: The action's error property and the HTTP return code contain more information about the failure."}, {"v": "actionStat:PotentialActionStatus", "n": "Potential Action Status", "d": "Description of an action that is supported.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: actionStat:PotentialActionStatus"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AgentSector', 'Types of sociological, economic, or political subdivision of society.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AgentSector', $j$[{"v": "agentSector:PrivateForProfit", "n": "Private For-Profit", "d": "Sector that contains privately-owned organizations that operate for profit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: agentSector:PrivateForProfit"}, {"v": "agentSector:PrivateNonProfit", "n": "Private Not-For-Profit", "d": "Sector that contains privately-owned organizations that operate on a non-profit basis.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: agentSector:PrivateNonProfit\ndct:description: These include both independent not-for-profit schools and those affiliated with a religious organization."}, {"v": "agentSector:Public", "n": "Public", "d": "Sector that contains government and quasi-government organizations.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: agentSector:Public"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AgentServiceType', 'Types of services offered by an agent.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AgentServiceType', $j$[{"v": "serviceType:AccreditService", "n": "Accredit Service", "d": "Agent service provides official authorization to, or approval of, a credential, organization or program based on prescribed standards or criteria.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:AccreditService"}, {"v": "serviceType:ApproveService", "n": "Approve Service", "d": "Agent service official accepts a credential or authorizes an organization to act or operate.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:ApproveService"}, {"v": "serviceType:OfferService", "n": "Offer Service", "d": "Agent service offers resources such as credentials, assessments, or learning opportunities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:OfferService"}, {"v": "serviceType:RecognizeService", "n": "Recognize Service", "d": "Agent service recommends, endorses, indicates preference for, or otherwise provides a positive judgment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:RecognizeService"}, {"v": "serviceType:RegulateService", "n": "Regulate Service", "d": "Agent service monitors and enforces legal requirements or standards.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:RegulateService"}, {"v": "serviceType:RenewService", "n": "Renew Service", "d": "Agent provides service to extend (renew) the validity of a credential.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:RenewService"}, {"v": "serviceType:RevokeService", "n": "Revoke Service", "d": "Agent provides service to end (revoke) the validity or operation of an awarded credential.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: serviceType:RevokeService"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AgreementCategory', 'Concepts classifying formal mechanisms used to recognize or transfer learning across organizations or programs.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AgreementCategory', $j$[{"v": "agreementCat:ArticulationAgreement", "n": "Articulation Agreement", "d": "A formal mechanism establishing course or program equivalencies for recognition and transfer of learning between organizations or programs.", "u": "Applicable only to Transfer Agreements.", "notes": "concept: agreementCat:ArticulationAgreement"}, {"v": "agreementCat:MemorandumOfUnderstanding", "n": "Memorandum of Understanding", "d": "A formal mechanism expressing parties’ intent to collaborate or recognize learning, which may precede or accompany specific agreements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: agreementCat:MemorandumOfUnderstanding"}, {"v": "agreementCat:MultipartyAgreement", "n": "Multiparty Agreement", "d": "An agreement with more than two parties.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: agreementCat:MultipartyAgreement"}, {"v": "agreementCat:StandingTransferArrangement", "n": "Standing Transfer Arrangement", "d": "A formal mechanism applying standardized recognition rules across defined sets of courses or programs.", "u": "Applicable only to Transfer Agreements.", "notes": "concept: agreementCat:StandingTransferArrangement"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('Alignment', 'Types of relationship that can be asserted as existing between nodes in frameworks.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:Alignment', $j$[{"v": "alignment:BroadMatch", "n": "Broad Match", "d": "Assertion indicates that the referenced concept is broader in some way than this concept.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:BroadMatch"}, {"v": "alignment:CloseMatch", "n": "Close Match", "d": "Assertion indicates that two concepts are sufficiently similar that they can be used interchangeably.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:CloseMatch"}, {"v": "alignment:ExactMatch", "n": "Exact Match", "d": "Indicates semantic similarity denoting an even higher degree of closeness than skos:closeMatch.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:ExactMatch"}, {"v": "alignment:NarrowMatch", "n": "Narrow Match", "d": "Assertion indicates that the referenced concept is narrower in some way than this concept.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:NarrowMatch"}, {"v": "alignment:NoMatch", "n": "No Match", "d": "Assertion indicating that there is no related concept in the target framework.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:NoMatch"}, {"v": "alignment:RelatedMatch", "n": "Related Match", "d": "Assertion indicating an associative, non-hierarchical relationship between the two concepts where neither is broader nor narrower than the other.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: alignment:RelatedMatch"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ArrayOperationCategory', 'Concepts describing an action to be taken on an array of values.', 'Used in CTDL for actions performed on arrays, lists or sets or values in order to obtain some other value.', 'scheme: ceterms:ArrayOperationCategory', $j$[{"v": "array:AllOf", "n": "All Of", "d": "All of the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:AllOf"}, {"v": "array:AnyOf", "n": "Any Of", "d": "Any (one or more) of the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:AnyOf"}, {"v": "array:CountDistinct", "n": "Count Distinct", "d": "The number of unique values; yields a number.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:CountDistinct"}, {"v": "array:Max", "n": "Maximum", "d": "The highest of all the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:Max"}, {"v": "array:Mean", "n": "Mean", "d": "The arithmetic mean of all the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:Mean"}, {"v": "array:Min", "n": "Minimum", "d": "The lowest of all the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:Min"}, {"v": "array:OneOf", "n": "One Of", "d": "Any one (but no more) of the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:OneOf"}, {"v": "array:Sum", "n": "Sum", "d": "The numeric total obtained by adding all the values.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: array:Sum"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AssessmentMethod', 'Types of assessment method.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AssessmentMethod', $j$[{"v": "assessMethod:Artifact", "n": "Artifact", "d": "Work or product created or produced by the person being assessed.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessMethod:Artifact\ndct:description: Artifact includes, but is not limited to, an academic paper, video documentary, computer software, music composition, choreography, novel, short story, journal article, news article, report, lesson plan, product design, portfolio, manufactured product, etc. Methods of evaluation may include multiple evaluators either individually or as an expert panel using general criteria or more structured rubrics whose scores are combined, etc. Criteria and methods of evaluation are often very similar to those for assessing a performance, without the facets specific to a live performance"}, {"v": "assessMethod:Exam", "n": "Exam", "d": "Mix of scored items presented in fixed or open response formats including qualifying and comprehensive exams.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessMethod:Exam\ndct:description: Exam includes, but is not limited to, multiple choice, true-false, written essay, short-answer, fill-in or oral response formats that could include measurements of reasoning, problem-solving, critical thinking."}, {"v": "assessMethod:Performance", "n": "Performance", "d": "Set of behaviors or actions assessed as demonstration of competencies where the assessment occurs either as the actions take place (i.e., live) or through review of recordings of those actions in a persistent media (e.g., video, audio, keystroke records, etc.)", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessMethod:Performance\ndct:description: Performance includes, but is not limited to, dance, music, teaching, acting, medical procedures, truck driving, manufacturing production, etc. Criteria include the categories and benchmarks on which the performance is assessed. Methods of evaluation can include multiple evaluators either individually or as an expert panel using general criteria or more structured rubrics whose scores are combined (e.g., assessing a dance performance, evaluating the performance of a medical procedure, truck driving procedure, manufacturing process such as machining)."}, {"v": "assessMethod:PortfolioEvaluation", "n": "Portfolio Evaluation", "d": "Assessment method that evaluates a learner’s portfolio of evidence to determine knowledge, skills, or competencies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessMethod:PortfolioEvaluation\nbroader: assessMethod:Artifact"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AssessmentUse', 'Types of Intended uses of an assessment.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AssessmentUse', $j$[{"v": "assessUse:Formative", "n": "Formative Assessment", "d": "Formal and informal assessment procedures conducted during the learning process to support intentional modification in teaching and learning activities in order to improve learner attainment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessUse:Formative"}, {"v": "assessUse:Summative", "n": "Summative Assessment", "d": "Assessment of learning at the end of an instructional unit to determine whether some established standard or benchmark has been achieved.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: assessUse:Summative"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('Audience', 'Types of audiences for which the resource being described is applicable or available.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:Audience
dct:description: If the resource is applicable or available for any type of audience, do not select anything.', $j$[{"v": "audience:Citizen", "n": "Citizen", "d": "Person who is a legally recognized subject of a particular nation, state, province, or commonwealth.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Citizen"}, {"v": "audience:CulturalEthnicMinority", "n": "Cultural/Ethnic Minority", "d": "Person who belongs to a cultural and/or ethnic minority group, relative to the surrounding population.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CulturalEthnicMinority"}, {"v": "audience:CurrentlyIncarcerated", "n": "Currently Incarcerated", "d": "Person who is currently incarcerated.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CurrentlyIncarcerated"}, {"v": "audience:CurrentMilitary", "n": "Current Military", "d": "Current member of a nation's military.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CurrentMilitary"}, {"v": "audience:CurrentMilitaryDependent", "n": "Current Military Dependent", "d": "Dependent (usually a child) of a current member of a nation's military.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CurrentMilitaryDependent"}, {"v": "audience:CurrentMilitarySpouse", "n": "Current Military Spouse", "d": "Spouse of a current member of a nation's military.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CurrentMilitarySpouse"}, {"v": "audience:CurrentStudent", "n": "Current Student", "d": "Student currently participating in a learning opportunity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:CurrentStudent"}, {"v": "audience:Displaced", "n": "Displaced", "d": "Person who has been displaced from their home or community.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Displaced"}, {"v": "audience:FormerlyIncarcerated", "n": "Formerly Incarcerated", "d": "Person who was formerly incarcerated.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerlyIncarcerated"}, {"v": "audience:FormerMember", "n": "Former Member", "d": "Former member of an organization, society, or recognized group.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerMember\ndct:description: Membership includes types of affiliation such as employment or other work relationships, enrollment at an educational institution etc."}, {"v": "audience:FormerMilitary", "n": "Former Military / Veteran", "d": "Veteran of military service.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerMilitary"}, {"v": "audience:FormerMilitaryDependent", "n": "Former Military Dependent", "d": "Former dependent (usually a child) of a veteran of a nation's military.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerMilitaryDependent"}, {"v": "audience:FormerMilitarySpouse", "n": "Former Military Spouse", "d": "Spouse of a veteran of a nation's military.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerMilitarySpouse"}, {"v": "audience:FormerStudent", "n": "Former Student / Alumni", "d": "Student who previously participated in a learning opportunity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FormerStudent"}, {"v": "audience:FullTime", "n": "Full-Time", "d": "Participation in a learning opportunity to an extent that meets the opportunity's requirements for full-time status.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FullTime"}, {"v": "audience:FutureMember", "n": "Future Member", "d": "Future member of an organization, society, or recognized group.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FutureMember\ndct:description: Membership includes types of affiliation such as employment or other work relationships, enrollment at an educational institution etc."}, {"v": "audience:FutureStudent", "n": "Future Student", "d": "Student who intends to participate in a learning opportunity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:FutureStudent"}, {"v": "audience:Homemaker", "n": "Homemaker", "d": "Person who provides unpaid services to family members in the home.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Homemaker"}, {"v": "audience:JobSeeker", "n": "Job Seeker", "d": "Person who is currently seeking work.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:JobSeeker\ndct:description: This includes new job seekers as well as those who already have work and are seeking other work."}, {"v": "audience:Member", "n": "Member", "d": "Current member of an organization, society, or recognized group.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Member\ndct:description: Membership includes types of affiliation such as employment or other work relationships, enrollment at an educational institution etc."}, {"v": "audience:NonCitizen", "n": "Non-Citizen", "d": "Person who is not a legally recognized subject of a particular nation, state, province, or commonwealth.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:NonCitizen"}, {"v": "audience:NonMember", "n": "Non-Member", "d": "Individual without membership status or privileges conferred by an organization, society, or recognized group.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:NonMember"}, {"v": "audience:NonResident", "n": "Non-Resident", "d": "Person whose primary residence is not in nation, state, province, or commonwealth of concern.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:NonResident"}, {"v": "audience:PartTime", "n": "Part-Time", "d": "Participation in a learning opportunity to an extent that meets the opportunity's requirements for part-time status.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:PartTime"}, {"v": "audience:PrivateEmployee", "n": "Private Employee", "d": "Person employed in the private sector.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:PrivateEmployee"}, {"v": "audience:PublicEmployee", "n": "Public Employee", "d": "Person employed in the public sector.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:PublicEmployee"}, {"v": "audience:Resident", "n": "Resident", "d": "Person whose permanent and principal home is in a particular nation, state, province, or commonwealth.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Resident"}, {"v": "audience:Unemployed", "n": "Unemployed", "d": "Person who is not employed.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Unemployed"}, {"v": "audience:Youth", "n": "Youth", "d": "Person roughly between the ages of 15 and 24.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audience:Youth"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('AudienceLevel', 'Types of levels in an academic or training progression expected of, or to be developed by, the typical person for the resource being described.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:AudienceLevel', $j$[{"v": "audLevel:AdvancedLevel", "n": "Advanced Level", "d": "Intended for those with significant experience or expertise where developmental expectations are staged for assessing knowledge, skills, or competencies beyond the novice and intermediate levels.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:AdvancedLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:AssociatesDegreeLevel", "n": "Associates Degree Level", "d": "Intended for those completing college/university-level programs within their first one to two years (lower-division) of post-secondary education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:AssociatesDegreeLevel\nbroader: audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 5 – Short-cycle tertiary education."}, {"v": "audLevel:BachelorsDegreeLevel", "n": "Bachelors Degree Level", "d": "Intended for those completing college/university-level programs within approximately three to four years where course work and activities advance skills from a lower-division or generalist level to an upper-division level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:BachelorsDegreeLevel\nbroader: audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 6 – Bachelor’s or equivalent level."}, {"v": "audLevel:BeginnerLevel", "n": "Beginner Level", "d": "Intended for novices or those with limited experience.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:BeginnerLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:DoctoralDegreeLevel", "n": "Doctoral Degree Level", "d": "Intended for those who have completed Bachelors and Masters degrees or their equivalent and who will be required to complete either independent research or a significant project or paper.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:DoctoralDegreeLevel\nbroader: audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 8 – Doctoral or equivalent level."}, {"v": "audLevel:EarlyChildhood", "n": "Early Childhood", "d": "Intended for children before the start of primary education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:EarlyChildhood\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 0 – Early childhood education."}, {"v": "audLevel:GraduateLevel", "n": "Graduate Level", "d": "Intended for those who enrolled in a degree program or other formal program above the baccalaureate level, such as a masters or doctoral degree program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:GraduateLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:IntermediateLevel", "n": "Intermediate Level", "d": "Intended for those with some experience, where knowledge, skills, and competency expectations are staged for development beyond novice-level and in preparation for a more advanced-level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:IntermediateLevel\ndct:description: An individual at this level has foundational competencies to function independently with occasional supervision."}, {"v": "audLevel:LowerDivisionLevel", "n": "Lower Division Level", "d": "Intended for those in the first half of an undergraduate level program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:LowerDivisionLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:LowerSecondary", "n": "Lower Secondary", "d": "Intended for those at the earlier stages of secondary education, building on primary education, typically with a more subject-oriented curriculum.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:LowerSecondary\nbroader: audLevel:SecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 2 – Lower secondary education."}, {"v": "audLevel:MastersDegreeLevel", "n": "Masters Degree Level", "d": "Intended for those who have completed a Bachelor's Degree or equivalent.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:MastersDegreeLevel\nbroader: audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 7 – Master’s or equivalent level."}, {"v": "audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel", "n": "Post-Secondary Level", "d": "Intended for those who have completed secondary level school programs or equivalent.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:PostSecondaryLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:Primary", "n": "Primary", "d": "Intended for those who are acquiring fundamental skills in reading, writing and mathematics and establishing a solid foundation for learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:Primary\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 1 – Primary education."}, {"v": "audLevel:ProfessionalLevel", "n": "Professional Level", "d": "Intended for those attending professional programs or equivalent, such as law or medicine.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:ProfessionalLevel\ndct:description: Other levels can typically be paired with Professional Level to refine a description of a level."}, {"v": "audLevel:RemedialLevel", "n": "Remedial Level", "d": "Intended for those who are under-prepared for learning at a particular level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:RemedialLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:SecondaryLevel", "n": "Secondary School or Equivalent", "d": "Intended for those attending secondary (high-school) level programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:SecondaryLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:UndergraduateLevel", "n": "Undergraduate Level", "d": "Intended for those who are enrolled in a degree program or other formal program at or below the baccalaureate, such as an associate’s degree, vocational, or technical program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:UndergraduateLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:UpperDivisionLevel", "n": "Upper Division Level", "d": "Intended for those in the second half of an undergraduate level program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:UpperDivisionLevel"}, {"v": "audLevel:UpperSecondary", "n": "Upper Secondary", "d": "Intended for those at the later stages of secondary education, preparing for tertiary education or employment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: audLevel:UpperSecondary\nbroader: audLevel:SecondaryLevel\ndct:description: Aligns to ISCED 2011 level 3 – Upper secondary education."}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ClaimType', 'Types of the claims supported by a verification service.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ClaimType', $j$[{"v": "claimType:BadgeClaim", "n": "Badge Claim", "d": "Verifiable visual representation that can be shared, embedded, linked, or otherwise used to publicly indicate that an individual has the represented credential.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: claimType:BadgeClaim"}, {"v": "claimType:QualityAssuranceClaim", "n": "Quality Assurance Claim", "d": "Verifiable representation of quality assurance.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: claimType:QualityAssuranceClaim"}, {"v": "claimType:TranscriptClaim", "n": "Transcript Claim", "d": "Verifiable representation of postsecondary courses and degrees completed.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: claimType:TranscriptClaim"}, {"v": "claimType:VerifiedClaim", "n": "Verified Claim", "d": "Verifiable representation of the credential holder's achievement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: claimType:VerifiedClaim"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('CollectionCategory', 'Types of collection, list, or array that groups together other resources.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:CollectionCategory', $j$[{"v": "collectionCategory:Competency", "n": "Competency", "d": "Aggregation of Competencies.", "u": "Use ceasn:CompetencyFramework for aggregations of competencies that are logically related.", "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:Competency"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:ETPL", "n": "Eligible Training Providers List", "d": "Training providers meeting the requirements stipulated in the U.S. Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:ETPL\ndct:description: This list includes the Learning Opportunities and Credentials offered by training providers that have met requirements."}, {"v": "collectionCategory:GIBill", "n": "GI Bill", "d": "Education and training programs qualifying for the U.S. GI Bill per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:GIBill"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:HighSkill", "n": "High Skill", "d": "Occupations, Jobs, Work Roles, or Tasks meeting skill level criteria based on labor market data per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:HighSkill"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:HighWage", "n": "High Wage", "d": "Occupations and Jobs meeting earnings threshold criteria based on labor market data per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:HighWage"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:InDemand", "n": "In Demand", "d": "Resources meeting workforce demand criteria based on labor market data per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:InDemand"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:IndustryRecognized", "n": "Industry Recognized", "d": "Learning Opportunities, Learning Programs, Courses, Assessments or Credentials recognized in one or more industries based on factors such as job market demand per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:IndustryRecognized"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:Perkins", "n": "Perkins", "d": "Credentials approved for funding under the U.S. Strengthening Career and Technical Education for the 21st Century Act (Perkins V) per the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:Perkins"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:PromiseScholarship", "n": "Promise Scholarship", "d": "Specified programs in eligible postsecondary educational institutions for which qualified students may receive a Promise Scholarship.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:PromiseScholarship"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:Quality", "n": "Quality", "d": "Learning Opportunities, Learning Programs, Courses, Assessments or Credentials that meet criteria for quality as determined by the promulgating body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:Quality"}, {"v": "collectionCategory:StateApprovedPostsecondary", "n": "State Approved Postsecondary Programs", "d": "Learning Opportunities, Learning Programs, Courses, Assessments or Credentials approved by a state agency to be offered within that state’s jurisdiction by postsecondary institutions.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: collectionCategory:StateApprovedPostsecondary"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ComparatorCategory', 'Concepts for comparing two values.', 'Used in CTDL constraints as values of the ceterms:comparator property to make a comparison that should yield true or false. In all cases the left source of data is compared to the right source, sometimes the comparison is made after an action is applied, e.g. finding the mean of several numbers.', 'scheme: ceterms:ComparatorCategory', $j$[{"v": "compare:EQ", "n": "Equal To", "d": "The value of the left is equal to the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:EQ"}, {"v": "compare:GT", "n": "Greater Than", "d": "The value of the left is greater than the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:GT"}, {"v": "compare:GTEQ", "n": "Greater Than or Equal To", "d": "The value of the left is greater than or equal to the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:GTEQ"}, {"v": "compare:LT", "n": "Less Than", "d": "The value of the left is less than the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:LT"}, {"v": "compare:LTEQ", "n": "Less Than or Equal To", "d": "The value of the left is less than or equal to the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:LTEQ"}, {"v": "compare:NEQ", "n": "Not Equal To", "d": "The value of the left is not equal to the value of the right.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: compare:NEQ"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('CostType', 'Entity that describes the types of costs related to earning or completing a credential, assessment, or learning opportunity.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:CostType', $j$[{"v": "costType:AggregateCost", "n": "Aggregate Cost", "d": "Sum of direct costs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:AggregateCost"}, {"v": "costType:Application", "n": "Application", "d": "Cost of applying for the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:Application"}, {"v": "costType:BackgroundCheck", "n": "Background Check", "d": "Cost for a background check.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:BackgroundCheck"}, {"v": "costType:Childcare", "n": "Childcare", "d": "Financial aid towards paying for supervision, care, and activities for children.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:Childcare"}, {"v": "costType:Consumables", "n": "Consumables", "d": "Cost for supplies or materials that are depleted or replaced.", "u": "For resources such as textbooks use costType:LearningResource.", "notes": "concept: costType:Consumables"}, {"v": "costType:EnrollmentFee", "n": "Enrollment Fee", "d": "Cost to enroll in the learning opportunity being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:EnrollmentFee"}, {"v": "costType:Equipment", "n": "Equipment", "d": "Cost for durable tools, instruments or machines.", "u": "For resources such as textbooks use costType:LearningResource.", "notes": "concept: costType:Equipment"}, {"v": "costType:GraduationFee", "n": "Graduation Fee", "d": "Separate graduation fee.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:GraduationFee"}, {"v": "costType:LearningResource", "n": "Learning Resource", "d": "Cost for one or more learning resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:LearningResource\ndct:description: Examples include resources such as textbooks, workbooks, laboratory supplies, and other related supplies."}, {"v": "costType:Meals", "n": "Meals", "d": "Cost for meals while participating in the learning opportunity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:Meals"}, {"v": "costType:MixedFees", "n": "Mixed Fees", "d": "The sum of fees that are not identified individually.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:MixedFees"}, {"v": "costType:OptionalCharges", "n": "Optional Charges", "d": "Cost for additional fees, other services, equipment, or facilities that are not required.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:OptionalCharges"}, {"v": "costType:PersonalExpenses", "n": "Personal Expenses", "d": "Cost for personal living or incidental expenses.", "u": "Where possible use a more specific Cost Type, such as costType:Travel or costType:Meals.", "notes": "concept: costType:PersonalExpenses"}, {"v": "costType:ProcessingFee", "n": "Processing Fee", "d": "Cost for processing or expediting information related to the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:ProcessingFee"}, {"v": "costType:ProgramSpecificFee", "n": "Program Specific Fee", "d": "Additional cost for participation with a specific program or course of study such as engineering, business, and nursing.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:ProgramSpecificFee"}, {"v": "costType:ReexaminationFee", "n": "Reexamination Fee", "d": "Cost for retaking an instance of the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:ReexaminationFee"}, {"v": "costType:RenewalFee", "n": "Maintenance Fee", "d": "Cost for maintenance or renewal of the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:RenewalFee"}, {"v": "costType:ReschedulingFee", "n": "Rescheduling Fee", "d": "Cost for rescheduling an instance of the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:ReschedulingFee"}, {"v": "costType:RoomOrResidency", "n": "Room or Residence", "d": "Cost for room, residence or boarding.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:RoomOrResidency"}, {"v": "costType:ScoringFee", "n": "Scoring Fee", "d": "Cost for scoring the resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:ScoringFee"}, {"v": "costType:SpecialHardship", "n": "Special Hardship", "d": "Financial aid towards covering hardship arising from unforeseen circumstances.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:SpecialHardship"}, {"v": "costType:SpecialNeeds", "n": "Special Needs", "d": "Financial aid towards paying for extra costs associated with accommodating a special need.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:SpecialNeeds"}, {"v": "costType:StandaloneAssessment", "n": "Standalone Assessment", "d": "Cost for standalone assessments.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:StandaloneAssessment"}, {"v": "costType:StudentServicesFee", "n": "Student Services Fee", "d": "Cost for student services related to the learning opportunity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:StudentServicesFee"}, {"v": "costType:TechnologyFee", "n": "Technology Fee", "d": "Cost for accessing technologies related to the learning opportunity or activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:TechnologyFee"}, {"v": "costType:Travel", "n": "Travel", "d": "Financial aid towards paying for travel costs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:Travel"}, {"v": "costType:Tuition", "n": "Tuition", "d": "Cost for teaching and instruction.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: costType:Tuition"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('CredentialStatus', 'Types of applicability statuses of a credential.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:CredentialStatus', $j$[{"v": "credentialStat:Active", "n": "Active", "d": "Awards of the credential are ongoing.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:Active"}, {"v": "credentialStat:Ceasing", "n": "Ceasing", "d": "Resource is in the process of becoming no longer active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:Ceasing"}, {"v": "credentialStat:Deprecated", "n": "Deprecated", "d": "Awards of the credential have ceased.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:Deprecated"}, {"v": "credentialStat:Probationary", "n": "Probationary", "d": "Credential award is provisional or temporary; frequently pending further assessment of qualification.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:Probationary"}, {"v": "credentialStat:Suspended", "n": "Suspended", "d": "Awards of the credential are not available, but may resume.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:Suspended"}, {"v": "credentialStat:TeachOut", "n": "Teach Out", "d": "Arrangement by which an educational institution provides its current students with the opportunity to complete the credential when the program, institution or location offering access closes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: credentialStat:TeachOut"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('CreditUnit', 'Broad descriptions of units used to measure credit associated with a resource.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:CreditUnit', $j$[{"v": "creditUnit:AcademicYear", "n": "Academic Year", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted as being related to one or more academic years.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:AcademicYear\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:CarnegieUnit", "n": "Carnegie Unit", "d": "Credit that is based on 120 hours of contact time or class time with an instructor.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:CarnegieUnit\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:CertificateCredit", "n": "Certificate Credit", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted for certificates.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:CertificateCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit\ndct:description: Includes credits earned while enrolled in a certificate program."}, {"v": "creditUnit:ClockHour", "n": "Clock Hour", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted as being related to one or more temporal hours.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:ClockHour\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:CompetencyCredit", "n": "Competency Credit", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted for a particular competency or set of competencies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:CompetencyCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:ContactHour", "n": "Contact Hour", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted as being related to one or more temporal hours of instruction presented to students.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:ContactHour\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:ContinuingEducationUnit", "n": "Continuing Education Unit", "d": "Credit that is issued or is accepted as education units for meeting professional development requirements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:ContinuingEducationUnit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit\ndct:description: Based on international standards, continuing education units are based on contact hours that may be converted to other units of measurement, such as professional development hours (PDH), continuing education credits (CEU), and continuing professional credits (CPC)."}, {"v": "creditUnit:DegreeCredit", "n": "Degree Credit", "d": "Credit that is issued or is accepted as credit for earning a college-level degree.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:DegreeCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit\ndct:description: Includes credits earned while enrolled in a postsecondary program for a college-level degree."}, {"v": "creditUnit:DualCredit", "n": "Dual Credit", "d": "Credit that is applicable to two different educational levels.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:DualCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:QuarterHour", "n": "Quarter Hour", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted at an academic quarter level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:QuarterHour\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:RequirementCredit", "n": "Requirement Credit", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted for some type of requirement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:RequirementCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:SecondaryDiplomaCredit", "n": "Secondary Diploma Credit", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted for a secondary diploma.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:SecondaryDiplomaCredit\nbroader: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit\ndct:description: Includes credits earned while enrolled in a secondary diploma program that meet graduation requirements."}, {"v": "creditUnit:SemesterHour", "n": "Semester Hour", "d": "Credit that is issued or accepted at a semester level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:SemesterHour\nbroader: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit", "n": "Time-Based Credit", "d": "Credit with a unit of measurement based on time, either figuratively or literally.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:TimeBasedCredit"}, {"v": "creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit", "n": "Type-Based Credit", "d": "Credit with a unit of measurement based on the type of credit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: creditUnit:TypeBasedCredit"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('Delivery', 'Types of technical form for providing instances of the entity.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:Delivery', $j$[{"v": "deliveryType:Asynchronous", "n": "Asynchronous", "d": "Delivery is such that participants are not expected to undertake activities simultaneously.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:Asynchronous"}, {"v": "deliveryType:BlendedDelivery", "n": "Blended Delivery", "d": "Delivery includes significant levels of both in person and online.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:BlendedDelivery"}, {"v": "deliveryType:InPerson", "n": "In-Person Only", "d": "Delivery is only face-to-face.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:InPerson"}, {"v": "deliveryType:MixedSynchronous", "n": "Mixed Synchronous", "d": "Delivery is such that participants are expected to undertake some, but not all, activities simultaneously.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:MixedSynchronous"}, {"v": "deliveryType:OnlineOnly", "n": "Online Only", "d": "Delivery is only via the Internet.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:OnlineOnly"}, {"v": "deliveryType:Synchronous", "n": "Synchronous", "d": "Delivery is such that participants are expected to undertake activities simultaneously.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:Synchronous"}, {"v": "deliveryType:VariableSite", "n": "Variable Site", "d": "Delivery is not tied to a specific site.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: deliveryType:VariableSite\ndct:description: Includes physical/in-person delivery to a range of locations, whether predetermined or customized to a specific need. Examples include equipment for dispensing information to mobile devices in locations with limited/no connection."}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ExternalInput', 'Types of external stakeholders that provide input to the process.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ExternalInput', $j$[{"v": "inputType:ArtificialIntelligence", "n": "Artificial Intelligence", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations based on, or provided by any form of AI.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:ArtificialIntelligence"}, {"v": "inputType:Associations", "n": "Professional Associations", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by professional associations.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Associations"}, {"v": "inputType:Business", "n": "Business", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by business.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Business"}, {"v": "inputType:BusinessAssociation", "n": "Business or Industry Association", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by business or industry association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:BusinessAssociation"}, {"v": "inputType:Committee", "n": "Committee", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by a group of individuals convened to represent a larger group or range of stakeholders.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Committee"}, {"v": "inputType:Consumers", "n": "Consumers", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by consumers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Consumers"}, {"v": "inputType:EducationAdministrators", "n": "Education Administrators", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by education administrators.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:EducationAdministrators"}, {"v": "inputType:Educators", "n": "Educators", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by education instructors or faculty.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Educators"}, {"v": "inputType:Experts", "n": "Subject Matter Experts", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by subject matter experts.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Experts"}, {"v": "inputType:Governments", "n": "Governments", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by government.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Governments\ndct:description: May include local, state or provincial, and federal or national government."}, {"v": "inputType:Guardians", "n": "Guardians", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by parents or guardians.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Guardians"}, {"v": "inputType:InternationalBodies", "n": "International Bodies", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by international bodies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:InternationalBodies"}, {"v": "inputType:Practitioners", "n": "Practitioners", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by practitioners.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Practitioners"}, {"v": "inputType:Public", "n": "Public", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by community members and the general public.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Public"}, {"v": "inputType:Students", "n": "Students", "d": "External stakeholder review, guidance or recommendations by all types of learners.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: inputType:Students"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('FinancialAssistance', 'Types of financial assistance typically available in the United States.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:FinancialAssistance', $j$[{"v": "financialAid:AcademicAssistantship", "n": "Academic Assistantship", "d": "Paid employment in which students receive tuition or other reimbursement for the tasks they perform for faculty members, departments, and/or educational institutions.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:AcademicAssistantship\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:Apprenticeship", "n": "Apprenticeship", "d": "Combination of on-the-job training and related instruction that meets standards in which workers learn the practical and theoretical aspects of a skilled occupation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Apprenticeship\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:CoOperative", "n": "Co-Operative", "d": "Paid work experience utilized by approved career and technical education programs to combine classroom and on-the-job training and education which provides academic credit for structured job experience.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:CoOperative\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:DoDTuitionAssistance", "n": "Department of Defense Tuition Assistance", "d": "Financial assistance provided to qualified active duty service members and their families for voluntary off-duty educational programs in support of professional and personal self-development goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:DoDTuitionAssistance\nbroader: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:FederalGrant", "n": "Federal Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, which doesn’t require repayment, based on meeting requirements determined by the Federal Government.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:FederalGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:FederalScholarship", "n": "Federal Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award, which doesn’t require repayment, from the Federal Government based on student achievement and other criteria for education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:FederalScholarship\nbroader: financialAid:Scholarship"}, {"v": "financialAid:FederalSubsidizedLoan", "n": "Federal Subsidized Loan", "d": "Loan from the Federal Government that is based on financial needs of the student and is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:FederalSubsidizedLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:FederalUnsubsidizedLoan", "n": "Federal Unsubsidized Loan", "d": "Loan from the Federal Government that does not require evidence of the financial needs of the student, and is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:FederalUnsubsidizedLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:FederalWorkStudy", "n": "Federal Work Study", "d": "Program funded by the Federal Government designed to provide part-time jobs for students to offset educational expenses.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:FederalWorkStudy\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:General", "n": "General Financial Assistance", "d": "Types of financial assistance for students towards education, training, or related costs of pursuing a credential, program, or other resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:General"}, {"v": "financialAid:Grant", "n": "Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, which doesn’t require repayment, based on meeting requirements determined by the grantor.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Grant\nbroader: financialAid:General"}, {"v": "financialAid:InstitutionalGrant", "n": "Institutional Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, including free or discounted tuition or other fees, which doesn’t require repayment, based on meeting requirements determined by an educational institution.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:InstitutionalGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:InstitutionalLoan", "n": "Institutional Loan", "d": "Loan from an educational institution that is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:InstitutionalLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:InstitutionalScholarship", "n": "Institutional Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award, which doesn’t require repayment, from an educational institution based on student achievement and other criteria for education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:InstitutionalScholarship\nbroader: financialAid:Scholarship"}, {"v": "financialAid:Internship", "n": "Internship", "d": "Time-limited work offered by an organization approved by a qualified institution to gain experience or satisfy requirements for another resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Internship\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:Loan", "n": "Loan", "d": "Financial aid that requires repayment with terms determined by the entity providing the loan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Loan\nbroader: financialAid:General"}, {"v": "financialAid:LoanForgivenessProgram", "n": "Loan Forgiveness Program", "d": "Program that forgives the remaining balance on a loan after meeting certain requirements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:LoanForgivenessProgram\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:Military", "n": "Military", "d": "Financial aid available to active duty service members, veterans, and/or their qualified family members.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:OtherGrant", "n": "Other Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy based on meeting requirements from one or more other sources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:OtherGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:OtherLoan", "n": "Other Loan", "d": "Loan from one or more other sources that is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:OtherLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:OtherOnCampusWork", "n": "Other On-Campus Work", "d": "Paid non-academic employment available for students on an educational institution’s campus.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:OtherOnCampusWork\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:OtherScholarship", "n": "Other Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award, which doesn’t require repayment, from one or more other sources based on student achievement and other criteria.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:OtherScholarship\nbroader: financialAid:Scholarship"}, {"v": "financialAid:ParentPLUSLoan", "n": "Parent PLUS Loan", "d": "Loan from the Federal Government available to the parents of dependent students.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:ParentPLUSLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:PellGrant", "n": "Pell Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, which doesn’t require repayment, that the Federal Government provides based on the financial needs of the student.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:PellGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:Post911GIBill", "n": "Post 9-11 GI Bill", "d": "Financial assistance provided to qualified active duty service members, veterans, and qualified family members that is based on military service and intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Post911GIBill\nbroader: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:PrivateGrant", "n": "Private Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, which doesn’t require repayment, based on meeting requirements determined by a private entity, including employers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:PrivateGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:PrivateLoan", "n": "Private Loan", "d": "Loan from a private entity, including employers, that is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:PrivateLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:PrivateScholarship", "n": "Private Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award, which doesn’t require repayment, from a private entity, including employers, based on student achievement and other criteria for education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:PrivateScholarship\nbroader: financialAid:Scholarship"}, {"v": "financialAid:PromiseProgram", "n": "Promise Program", "d": "Program for students in a given area, with minimal requirements, that pays for tuition without requiring repayment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:PromiseProgram\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:Scholarship", "n": "Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award based on student achievement and other criteria for education that doesn’t require repayment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Scholarship\nbroader: financialAid:General"}, {"v": "financialAid:StateLocalGrant", "n": "State or Local Grant", "d": "Financial subsidy, which doesn’t require repayment, based on meeting requirements determined by a state, province, region, and/or local government.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:StateLocalGrant\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:StateLocalLoan", "n": "State or Local Loan", "d": "Loan from a state, province, region, and/or local government that is intended to offset costs related to education, living, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:StateLocalLoan\nbroader: financialAid:Loan"}, {"v": "financialAid:StateLocalMilitaryAssistance", "n": "State or Local Military Assistance", "d": "Financial aid provided by a state or local government to active duty service members, veterans, and/or qualified family members.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:StateLocalMilitaryAssistance\nbroader: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:StateLocalScholarship", "n": "State or Local Scholarship", "d": "Financial aid award, which doesn’t require repayment, from a state, province, region, and/or local government based on student achievement and other criteria for education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:StateLocalScholarship\nbroader: financialAid:Scholarship"}, {"v": "financialAid:StateLocalWork", "n": "State or Local Work", "d": "Program funded by a state, province, region, and/or local government designed to provide work for students to offset educational expenses.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:StateLocalWork\nbroader: financialAid:WorkBased"}, {"v": "financialAid:Stipend", "n": "Stipend", "d": "A fixed sum of money paid for services or to defray expenses incurred through specific activities, which is typically distinct from wages or a salary.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:Stipend\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:VEAP", "n": "Veteran Educational Assistance Program", "d": "Financial assistance provided to qualified active duty service members and veterans as a matching program that is intended to offset educational expenses.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:VEAP\nbroader: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:VocationalRehabilitation", "n": "Vocational Rehabilitation", "d": "Financial for veterans with a qualifying service-connected disability rating for training or education related to pursuit of a career or career-related resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:VocationalRehabilitation\nbroader: financialAid:Military"}, {"v": "financialAid:WIOA", "n": "Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act (WIOA)", "d": "Financial aid established on behalf of a qualified participant with a training provider that is on the state's Eligible Training Provider List (ETPL).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:WIOA\nbroader: financialAid:Grant"}, {"v": "financialAid:WorkBased", "n": "Work-Based", "d": "Financial compensation for participating in work-based learning opportunities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: financialAid:WorkBased\nbroader: financialAid:General"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('Format', 'Types of file format, based on MIME types.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:Format', $j$[{"v": "format:plainText", "n": "Plain Text", "d": "Plain text, equivalent to the text/plain MIME type.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: format:plainText"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LearningMethod', 'Types of methods used to conduct the learning opportunity.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LearningMethod', $j$[{"v": "learnMethod:Applied", "n": "Applied Instruction", "d": "Provides learning opportunities in the context of real world examples, cases, and applications.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Applied\ndct:description: Applies to methods such as contextual learning, applied academics, academic-technical integration, problem-based learning, project-based learning, and case methods."}, {"v": "learnMethod:Apprenticeship", "n": "Apprenticeship", "d": "Learning through work that leads to a credential that is recognized by a relevant authority and is deliberately structured and supported to provide a progression of learning experiences.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Apprenticeship\nbroader: learnMethod:WorkBased"}, {"v": "learnMethod:AugmentedReality", "n": "Augmented Reality", "d": "Provides interactive learning experience through technology that superimposes a computer-generated image on a user's view of the real world, thus providing a composite view.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:AugmentedReality"}, {"v": "learnMethod:ClinicalRotation", "n": "Clinical Rotation", "d": "Learning through real-world work experience in a medical context under the direct supervision of a qualified practitioner.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:ClinicalRotation\nbroader: learnMethod:WorkBased"}, {"v": "learnMethod:CocurricularLearning", "n": "Cocurricular Learning", "d": "Learning opportunity that supplements or complements the curriculum.", "u": "Use for activities that are not part of a formal curriculum.", "notes": "concept: learnMethod:CocurricularLearning"}, {"v": "learnMethod:CohortBased", "n": "Cohort-Based", "d": "Format in which people  progress as a group.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:CohortBased"}, {"v": "learnMethod:CompetencyBased", "n": "Competency Based", "d": "Method that focuses on learners demonstrating the knowledge, skills and/or attitudes in highly specific units regardless of time, place, or pace of learning, usually in authentic contexts.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:CompetencyBased\ndct:description: This definition is based on Commonwealth of Learning (COL) \"Open and Distance Learning: Key Terms and Definitions\" (May 2023) http://hdl.handle.net/11599/3558"}, {"v": "learnMethod:Gaming", "n": "Gaming", "d": "Provides interactive educational experiences which demonstrate concepts in a way that promotes critical thinking, overcoming challenges within prescribed rule sets, problem solving, and in some cases, teamwork and/or competition.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Gaming\ndct:description: Individual or group games that have cognitive, social, behavioral, and/or emotional dimensions which are related to educational objectives."}, {"v": "learnMethod:InstructorLed", "n": "Instructor-Led", "d": "Learning activities are facilitated by a subject matter expert.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:InstructorLed\ndct:description: The subject matter expert is expected to be a human and may be known as an instructor, teacher, trainer."}, {"v": "learnMethod:Internship", "n": "Internship", "d": "Work position that is intended to provide a learner with an opportunity to gain experience but that is not structured around learning and does not itself lead to a credential recognized by a relevant authority.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Internship\nbroader: learnMethod:WorkBased"}, {"v": "learnMethod:Laboratory", "n": "Laboratory", "d": "Hands-on individual or group experiences for applied learning concepts and methods, procedures and protocols with equipment and technologies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Laboratory\ndct:description: Applies to clinical practice and methods such as physical and/or virtual simulation or participation, whether direct or indirect."}, {"v": "learnMethod:Lecture", "n": "Lecture", "d": "Primary method is presentation by an instructor of learning material and may include student discussion.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Lecture\ndct:description: Lecture courses may involve student questions and answers, but the role of the instructor is clearly differentiated from that of the students."}, {"v": "learnMethod:MedicalResidency", "n": "Medical Residency", "d": "Learning through real-world work experience at the graduate level in a medical context where a qualified participant works under the direct supervision of a senior practicioner.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:MedicalResidency\nbroader: learnMethod:WorkBased"}, {"v": "learnMethod:Prerecorded", "n": "Prerecorded", "d": "Learning by using video, audio, or other prerecorded content.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Prerecorded"}, {"v": "learnMethod:SelfPaced", "n": "Self Paced", "d": "Provides for personalization and flexibility in the timing and progression of learning for individual learners based on their preferences and needs, prior learning experiences, and ability to progress through learning opportunities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:SelfPaced\ndct:description: Applies to methods such as competency-based education, open-entry/open exit, independent study, private study, and correspondence."}, {"v": "learnMethod:Seminar", "n": "Seminar", "d": "Primary method is active student discussion leading to advancement of the topic and facilitated by an instructor.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Seminar\ndct:description: Seminars typically involve small groups to facilitate equal opportunity with the instructor and colleagues to be engaged and occasionally may include students leading discussions."}, {"v": "learnMethod:Simulation", "n": "Simulation", "d": "Provides interactive learning experience through imitation of a situation or process.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:Simulation"}, {"v": "learnMethod:WorkBased", "n": "Work Based", "d": "Provides real-world work experiences that may be paid or unpaid and provided in group or individual formats normally outside the classroom.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: learnMethod:WorkBased\ndct:description: Applies to methods such as apprenticeships, internships, externships, work study, clinical rotations, residencies, practicums, field study, team projects, and cooperative education."}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LearningRecognitionEvidenceCategory', 'Concepts describing types of evidence accepted for learning recognition evaluation.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LearningRecognitionEvidenceCategory', $j$[{"v": "lrEvidence:AssessmentScore", "n": "Assessment Score", "d": "Official documentation of a person’s assessment results.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:AssessmentScore"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:CompletionRecord", "n": "Completion Record", "d": "Document verifying successful completion of structured training with an identifiable provider.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:CompletionRecord\ndct:description: Applies to employer, community-based, military, or continuing education training."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:Credential", "n": "Credential", "d": "Representation of a credential, digital or non-digital, attesting to a person’s achievements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:Credential"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:CreditRecommendation", "n": "Credit Recommendation", "d": "Recommendation for credit or competency value issued by an authoritative evaluating body, including amount, level, and conditions for specified learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:CreditRecommendation\ndct:description: In the U.S., common sources include ACE credit recommendations."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:EmployerAttestation", "n": "Employer Attestation", "d": "Formal statement from an employer verifying duties, scope of work, and performance relevant to claimed learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:EmployerAttestation"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:HoursVerification", "n": "Hours Verification", "d": "Record confirming supervised practice, clinical hours, or comparable time-based experience.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:HoursVerification\ndct:description: Common in clinical, practicum, apprenticeship, or licensure contexts."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:JobVerification", "n": "Job Verification", "d": "Official role description with verification of incumbency and dates.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:JobVerification"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:MilitaryTranscript", "n": "Military Transcript", "d": "Official record of a person’s military education, training, occupations, and related evaluations.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:MilitaryTranscript"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:Portfolio", "n": "Portfolio", "d": "Curated collection of artifacts evidencing learning typically aligned to defined outcomes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:Portfolio"}, {"v": "lrEvidence:ReflectiveNarrative", "n": "Reflective Narrative", "d": "Structured reflection connecting prior experience to defined competencies or outcomes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:ReflectiveNarrative\ndct:description: Often required in portfolio submissions. There may be a requirement for commentary or analysis in the narrative."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:ResumeVerification", "n": "Résumé Verification", "d": "Structured record of experience and education accompanied by sufficient validation for evaluation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:ResumeVerification\ndct:description: Validation may include references, verification letters, or linked evidence."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:SkillProfile", "n": "Skill Profile", "d": "Document that maps a person’s work artifacts or experiences to specified competencies, learning outcomes, or course requirements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:SkillProfile\ndct:description: Improves defensibility and transparency."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:Syllabus", "n": "Syllabus", "d": "Document outlining objectives, content, requirements, schedule, and assessment for a specific course.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:Syllabus\ndct:description: Supports content and outcome alignment."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:Transcript", "n": "Transcript", "d": "Official academic record of a person’s achievements issued by the record holder.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:Transcript\ndct:description: May be issued by the originating institution or a recognized clearinghouse."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:WorkplaceLearningRecord", "n": "Workplace Learning Record", "d": "Documentation of a person's on the job learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:WorkplaceLearningRecord\ndct:description: Includes Apprentice Logbooks and similar."}, {"v": "lrEvidence:WorkProduct", "n": "Work Product", "d": "Substantive work product demonstrating applied knowledge aligned to defined outcomes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrEvidence:WorkProduct\ndct:description: May include reports, designs, code, media, or presentations."}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LearningRecognitionMethodCategory', 'Concepts describing methods used to evaluate and recognize learning.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LearningRecognitionMethodCategory', $j$[{"v": "lrMethod:CreditRecommendationReview", "n": "Credit Recommendation Review", "d": "An evaluation method that uses an authoritative body’s credit recommendation to determine credit awards.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:CreditRecommendationReview\ndct:description: In the U.S., examples include American Council on Education (ACE) credit recommendations."}, {"v": "lrMethod:ExternalTrainingEvaluation", "n": "External Training Evaluation", "d": "An evaluation method in which structured, external non-academic training is reviewed to award credit or standing.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:ExternalTrainingEvaluation\ndct:description: May be conducted by employer, third-party, vendor, or external credentialing organization."}, {"v": "lrMethod:FacultyDevelopedExamination", "n": "Faculty-Developed Examination", "d": "A method in which learning is assessed by a course-specific exam created and administered by faculty.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:FacultyDevelopedExamination\ndct:description: In the United States, examples include challenge exams."}, {"v": "lrMethod:FacultyTransferEvaluation", "n": "Faculty Transfer Evaluation", "d": "An evaluation method in which faculty subject-matter experts judge whether prior learning meets course outcomes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:FacultyTransferEvaluation"}, {"v": "lrMethod:IndividualizedPriorLearningAssessment", "n": "Individualized Prior Learning Assessment", "d": "An evaluation method that uses personalized approaches to assess learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:IndividualizedPriorLearningAssessment\ndct:description: Examples include portfolio review, simulation, and interview."}, {"v": "lrMethod:InstitutionDevelopedAssessment", "n": "Institution-Developed Assessment", "d": "A method in which institution-created assessments are used to determine credit for prior learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:InstitutionDevelopedAssessment\ndct:description: Examples include challenge exams, projects, and labs."}, {"v": "lrMethod:InternationalCreditEvaluation", "n": "International Credit Evaluation", "d": "An evaluation method in which learning or credit earned from organizations in other countries is reviewed for recognition.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:InternationalCreditEvaluation"}, {"v": "lrMethod:PortfolioAssessment", "n": "Portfolio Assessment", "d": "A method in which a learner-developed portfolio is assessed to evidence prior learning aligned to defined outcomes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:PortfolioAssessment\ndct:description: Examples include documentation, work products, and artifacts mapped to competencies or requirements."}, {"v": "lrMethod:PriorLearningAssessment", "n": "Prior Learning Assessment", "d": "A structured method used to evaluate an individual's prior learning and its applicability to requirements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:PriorLearningAssessment"}, {"v": "lrMethod:ProficiencyExamination", "n": "Proficiency Examination", "d": "A method in which learning is assessed by an exam used to demonstrate subject mastery for placement or credit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:ProficiencyExamination\ndct:description: May be internal or external; use Standardized Examination when using recognized national/international exams."}, {"v": "lrMethod:StandardizedExamination", "n": "Standardized Examination", "d": "A method in which learning is assessed by a recognized standardized exam administered by an authoritative body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:StandardizedExamination\ndct:description: In the United States, examples include AP, CLEP, DLPT."}, {"v": "lrMethod:TranscriptEvaluation", "n": "Transcript Evaluation", "d": "An evaluation method in which prior records are reviewed to determine applicability.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:TranscriptEvaluation"}, {"v": "lrMethod:TransferCreditEvaluation", "n": "Transfer Credit Evaluation", "d": "An evaluation method that provides a preliminary determination of transferability using supplied records before matriculation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrMethod:TransferCreditEvaluation"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LearningRecognitionOutcomeCategory', 'Concepts describing outcomes of learning recognition.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LearningRecognitionOutcomeCategory', $j$[{"v": "lrOutcome:AdvancedStanding", "n": "Advanced Standing", "d": "An outcome in which standing toward a program or qualification is granted, which may or may not carry transcripted credit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:AdvancedStanding"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:CreditAwarded", "n": "Credit Awarded", "d": "An outcome in which learning results in transcripted credit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:CreditAwarded"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:CreditEquivalency", "n": "Credit Equivalency", "d": "An outcome in which learning fulfills a credit requirement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:CreditEquivalency"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:EligibilityMet", "n": "Eligibility Met", "d": "An outcome in which a prerequisite, admission, or other eligibility requirement is satisfied by recognized learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:EligibilityMet"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:ExemptionWaiver", "n": "Exemption Waiver", "d": "An outcome in which a requirement is waived.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:ExemptionWaiver"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:NotRecognized", "n": "Not Recognized", "d": "An outcome in which an evaluation is completed but no recognition is granted.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:NotRecognized"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:Placement", "n": "Placement", "d": "An outcome in which a person is placed into a program, hired or promoted.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:Placement"}, {"v": "lrOutcome:RecognitionOnly", "n": "Recognition Only", "d": "An outcome in which learning is acknowledged for placement, exemption, or eligibility without awarding credit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrOutcome:RecognitionOnly"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LearningRecognitionSourceCategory', 'Concepts describing formal, non-formal, or informal contexts from which learning may be recognized for applicability toward requirements.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LearningRecognitionSourceCategory', $j$[{"v": "lrSource:Apprenticeship", "n": "Apprenticeship", "d": "Learning completed in a registered apprenticeship program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:Apprenticeship"}, {"v": "lrSource:ClinicalPracticum", "n": "Clinical Practicum", "d": "Learning acquired through supervised clinical or practicum experiences in applied professional settings aligned to program or licensure standards.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:ClinicalPracticum"}, {"v": "lrSource:CommunityBasedOrganizationTraining", "n": "Community-Based Organization Training", "d": "Learning completed through structured training delivered by a community-based organization.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:CommunityBasedOrganizationTraining"}, {"v": "lrSource:CommunityService", "n": "Community Service", "d": "Learning acquired through unpaid service activities performed for the benefit of a community or organization outside a formal curriculum or assessed program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:CommunityService"}, {"v": "lrSource:ContinuingEducation", "n": "Continuing Education", "d": "Learning completed through structured, non-degree continuing education coursework.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:ContinuingEducation"}, {"v": "lrSource:CooperativeEducation", "n": "Cooperative Education", "d": "Learning acquired through extended, alternating work–study placements integrated with an academic program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:CooperativeEducation"}, {"v": "lrSource:Course", "n": "Course", "d": "Learning completed in a course, a structured sequence of educational activities designed to develop prescribed competencies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:Course"}, {"v": "lrSource:CustodialEducation", "n": "Custodial Education", "d": "Learning completed in educational programs while an individual is incarcerated or in custody.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:CustodialEducation"}, {"v": "lrSource:Degree", "n": "Degree", "d": "Learning recognized on the basis of a previously awarded academic degree.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:Degree"}, {"v": "lrSource:DualEnrollment", "n": "Dual Enrollment", "d": "Learning completed in college-level coursework taken concurrently with secondary enrollment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:DualEnrollment"}, {"v": "lrSource:EmploymentBasedTraining", "n": "Employment-Based Training", "d": "Learning completed through formal training provided by an employer or workforce development program.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:EmploymentBasedTraining"}, {"v": "lrSource:Exam", "n": "Exam", "d": "Learning demonstrated via a recognized examination administered by a national, international, or military body.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:Exam"}, {"v": "lrSource:ExperientialLearning", "n": "Experiential Learning", "d": "Learning acquired through direct, hands-on experience with guided reflection in real or simulated settings.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lrSource:ExperientialLearning"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LifeCycleStatus', 'Types of states of a resource in terms of its stage in a life cycle.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:LifeCycleStatus', $j$[{"v": "lifeCycle:Active", "n": "Active", "d": "Resource is active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:Active"}, {"v": "lifeCycle:Ceased", "n": "Ceased", "d": "Resource is permanently no longer active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:Ceased"}, {"v": "lifeCycle:Ceasing", "n": "Ceasing", "d": "Resource is in the process of becoming no longer active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:Ceasing"}, {"v": "lifeCycle:Developing", "n": "Developing", "d": "Resource is under development and may or may not become active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:Developing"}, {"v": "lifeCycle:Suspended", "n": "Suspended", "d": "Resource is temporarily not active, current, ongoing, offered, operational, or available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:Suspended"}, {"v": "lifeCycle:TeachOut", "n": "Teach Out", "d": "Arrangement by which an educational institution provides its current students with the opportunity to complete their course of study when the program, institution or location offering access closes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: lifeCycle:TeachOut\nbroader: lifeCycle:Ceasing"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('LogicalOperatorCategory', 'Logical operators applicable to two or more items.', 'Used in CTDL for types of logical operator for combining two or more nested ComponentCondition entities, Constraint entities, or a mix of ComponentCondition and Constraint entities.', 'scheme: ceterms:LogicalOperatorCategory', $j$[{"v": "logic:And", "n": "And", "d": "Relation is satisfied when all of the conditions and constraints are satisfied.", "u": "When used in a Component Condition, this applies to the combination of all immediately subordinate Component Conditions and Constraints.", "notes": "concept: logic:And"}, {"v": "logic:OnlyOne", "n": "Only One", "d": "Relation is satisfied when exactly one, and not more, of the conditions or constraints is satisfied.", "u": "When used in a Component Condition, this applies to the combination of all immediately subordinate Component Conditions and Constraints.", "notes": "concept: logic:OnlyOne"}, {"v": "logic:Or", "n": "Or", "d": "Relation is satisfied when at least one of the conditions or constraints is satisfied.", "u": "When used in a Component Condition, this applies to the combination of all immediately subordinate Component Conditions and Constraints.", "notes": "concept: logic:Or"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('OrganizationType', 'Types of organization.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:OrganizationType', $j$[{"v": "orgType:AccreditationBody", "n": "Accreditation Body", "d": "Organization that evaluates other resources such as organizations, learning opportunities, credentials, and/or individuals to issue third-party validation that the resource meets certain standards of quality, competency, and integrity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:AccreditationBody\nbroader: orgType:QualityAssurance"}, {"v": "orgType:AssessmentBody", "n": "Assessment Body", "d": "Primarily offers assessments for credentials as a service.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:AssessmentBody"}, {"v": "orgType:Business", "n": "Business", "d": "Organization that primarily sells products or services and employs one or more individuals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Business"}, {"v": "orgType:BusinessAssociation", "n": "Business or Industry Association", "d": "Membership organization primarily engaged in promoting the interests of their business members and providing them with services that may involve the provision of education and credentialing services.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:BusinessAssociation"}, {"v": "orgType:CertificationBody", "n": "Certification Body", "d": "Independent, third-party organization that operates a certification program. A certification body may or may not be governmental, and may or may not have regulatory authority.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:CertificationBody"}, {"v": "orgType:Collaborative", "n": "Collaborative", "d": "Organized group of entities in the public, private, government sectors that collaborates to achieve a common set of goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Collaborative"}, {"v": "orgType:CoordinatingBody", "n": "Coordinating Body", "d": "An organization that organizes multiple stakeholders around a common goal.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:CoordinatingBody"}, {"v": "orgType:FourYear", "n": "Four-Year College", "d": "Authorized postsecondary institution that primarily offers bachelor or higher degrees, but may also award associate degrees.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:FourYear\nbroader: orgType:Postsecondary\ndct:description: Includes free-standing medical, law or other first-professional schools, schools that offer postbaccalaureate certificates only, those that offer graduate programs only, etc."}, {"v": "orgType:Government", "n": "Government Agency", "d": "Organization in the public sector at the federal, state or local levels.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Government\ndct:description: Includes quasi-governmental organizations, special districts (e.g., libraries), corrections organizations, etc., except college and school districts. Is also responsible for the oversight and administration of specific functions other than the military services."}, {"v": "orgType:HighSchool", "n": "High School", "d": "Secondary school providing instruction and educational services that do not focus primarily on career and technical education or alternative education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:HighSchool\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:LaborUnion", "n": "Labor Union", "d": "Membership organization of workers formed for the purpose of advancing its members' interests in respect to wages, benefits, and working conditions.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:LaborUnion"}, {"v": "orgType:LowerSecondarySchool", "n": "Lower Secondary School", "d": "School primarily offering programs at the first stage of secondary education building on primary education, typically with a more subject-oriented curriculum.", "u": "Use for Middle School.", "notes": "concept: orgType:LowerSecondarySchool\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:Magnet", "n": "Magnet/Competitive Admissions School", "d": "Public school offering special instruction and programs not available elsewhere, designed to attract a more diverse student body from throughout a school district.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Magnet\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:Military", "n": "Military", "d": "Armed services of a government entity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Military"}, {"v": "orgType:NonTraditional", "n": "Alternative/Non-Traditional School", "d": "Secondary (i.e., high school) that: 1) addresses needs of students which cannot typically be met in a regular school; 2) provides nontraditional education; 3) falls outside of the categories of regular, magnet/special program emphasis, or career and technical education.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:NonTraditional\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:Postsecondary", "n": "Postsecondary Educational Institution", "d": "Organization such as a college or university.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Postsecondary\ndct:description: Organization with the authority to award degrees, and whose primary purpose is to provide postsecondary (tertiary or non-tertiary) education including programs whose purpose is providing academic, vocational, and continuing professional education."}, {"v": "orgType:PrimarilyOnline", "n": "Primarily Online", "d": "Organization that primarily operates online.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:PrimarilyOnline"}, {"v": "orgType:PrimarySchool", "n": "Primary School", "d": "School primarily offering programs designed to provide students with fundamental skills in reading, writing and mathematics and to establish a solid foundation for learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:PrimarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:ProfessionalAssociation", "n": "Professional Association", "d": "Membership organization primarily engaged in promoting the interests of a particular profession, the interests of individuals engaged in that profession, and providing them with services that may involve the provision of education and credentialing services.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:ProfessionalAssociation"}, {"v": "orgType:QualityAssurance", "n": "Quality Assurance Body", "d": "External body that performs accreditation, endorsement, approval, and/or recognition of a credential issuer.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:QualityAssurance"}, {"v": "orgType:Regulator", "n": "Regulator", "d": "Organization that regulates other resources such as organizations, learning opportunities, credentials, and/or individuals against established standards and criteria.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Regulator\nbroader: orgType:QualityAssurance"}, {"v": "orgType:SecondarySchool", "n": "Secondary School", "d": "School offering programs at all levels of secondary education, building on primary education through to preparing for tertiary education or providing skills relevant to employment.", "u": "Use for schools that cover both Lower and Upper Secondary levels.", "notes": "concept: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:Technical", "n": "Career and Technical School", "d": "Secondary school that focuses primarily on providing formal preparation for skilled, technical or professional occupations or careers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Technical\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:TrainingProvider", "n": "Education and Training Provider", "d": "Organization whose major purpose is to provide education and training services but is not a postsecondary education institution with the authority to award degrees.", "u": "In the U.S., use for Title IV eligible organizations that do not award degrees.", "notes": "concept: orgType:TrainingProvider\ndct:description: Includes community-based organizations, non-degree granting proprietary schools which are education and training providers that are recognized by states as schools."}, {"v": "orgType:TwoYear", "n": "Two-Year College", "d": "Authorized postsecondary institution that primarily offers associate degrees and certificates, and, if authorized, may also award higher degrees.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:TwoYear\nbroader: orgType:Postsecondary\ndct:description: Includes occupational and vocational schools with programs of at least 1800 hours, academic institutions with programs of less than 4 years, etc."}, {"v": "orgType:UpperSecondarySchool", "n": "Upper Secondary School", "d": "School primarily offering programs at the final stage of secondary education preparing for tertiary education or providing skills relevant to employment, usually with an increased range of subject options and streams.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:UpperSecondarySchool\nbroader: orgType:SecondarySchool"}, {"v": "orgType:Vendor", "n": "Vendor", "d": "Sells, maintains, and issues credentials for its own products and services for public access and use.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: orgType:Vendor"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('PathwayType', 'Types of pathway sets used to indicate the purpose and nature of the collection of pathways.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:PathwayType', $j$[{"v": "pathwayType:CommonDestination", "n": "Common Destination", "d": "The pathways in the set share the same destination.", "u": "May be useful for describing different ways of achieving an outcome depending on the individuals current situation.", "notes": "concept: pathwayType:CommonDestination"}, {"v": "pathwayType:CommonOrigin", "n": "Common Origin", "d": "The pathways in the set share the same origin.", "u": "May be useful for describing different outcomes that may be reached after starting a learning opportunity or career pathway.", "notes": "concept: pathwayType:CommonOrigin"}, {"v": "pathwayType:MultipleDestinations", "n": "Multiple Destinations", "d": "The pathways in the set reach different destinations.", "u": "May be useful for describing different outcomes that may be reached after starting a learning opportunity or career pathway.", "notes": "concept: pathwayType:MultipleDestinations"}, {"v": "pathwayType:MultipleOrigins", "n": "Multiple Origins", "d": "The pathways in the set start from different origins.", "u": "May be useful for describing different ways of achieving an outcome depending on the individuals current situation.", "notes": "concept: pathwayType:MultipleOrigins"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('Residency', 'Types of residency.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:Residency', $j$[{"v": "residency:InState", "n": "In-State", "d": "Legal residency or domicile status of the agent is the state or province of the relevant activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: residency:InState"}, {"v": "residency:International", "n": "Foreign/International", "d": "Legal residency, domicile, or citizen status of the agent is as a foreign national.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: residency:International"}, {"v": "residency:Local", "n": "Local", "d": "Legal residency or domicile status of the agent is local.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: residency:Local"}, {"v": "residency:OutOfState", "n": "Out-of-State", "d": "Legal residency or domicile status of the agent is a state or province different from the state or provincial locus of the relevant activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: residency:OutOfState"}, {"v": "residency:Regional", "n": "Regional", "d": "Legal residency or domicile status of the agent is the same geographic or political region as that of the relevant activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: residency:Regional"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ScheduleFrequency', 'Types for how often events occur.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ScheduleFrequency', $j$[{"v": "scheduleFrequency:Annually", "n": "Annually", "d": "Schedule is on an annual basis, typically occurring once per year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Annually"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:BiMonthly", "n": "Bi-Monthly", "d": "Schedule is on a bi-monthly basis, typically occurring every other month.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:BiMonthly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:BiWeekly", "n": "Bi-Weekly", "d": "Schedule is on a bi-weekly basis, typically occurring every other week.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:BiWeekly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Daily", "n": "Daily", "d": "Schedule is on a daily basis, typically occurring once per day.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Daily"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:EventBased", "n": "Event-Based", "d": "Schedule is determined or triggered by other events, such as completion of activities, completion of the resource, events external to the resource, or other events; refer to the resource's information for details.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:EventBased"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Hourly", "n": "Hourly", "d": "Schedule is on a hourly basis, typically occurring once per hour.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Hourly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Irregular", "n": "Irregular", "d": "Schedule has no significant pattern.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Irregular"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Monthly", "n": "Monthly", "d": "Schedule is on a monthly basis, typically occurring once per month.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Monthly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:MultiplePerWeek", "n": "Multiple Per Week", "d": "Schedule is more frequent than a weekly basis.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:MultiplePerWeek"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:OnDemand", "n": "On-Demand", "d": "Schedule allows the participant to choose when the resource begins.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:OnDemand"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:OpenEntryExit", "n": "Open Entry/Exit", "d": "Schedule allows for the participant to enter, participate with, and complete the resource during any period of the resource's run time.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:OpenEntryExit"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Quarterly", "n": "Quarterly", "d": "Schedule is on an quarterly basis, typically occurring three or four times per year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Quarterly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:SelfPaced", "n": "Self-Paced", "d": "Schedule allows for participation at a self-determined pace, though some specific dates and deadlines may be involved.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:SelfPaced"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:SemiAnnually", "n": "Semi-Annually", "d": "Schedule is on an semi-annual basis, typically occurring twice per year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:SemiAnnually"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:SemiMonthly", "n": "Semi-Monthly", "d": "Schedule is on a semi-monthly basis, typically occurring twice per month.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:SemiMonthly"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:SingleInstance", "n": "Single Instance", "d": "Schedule is a single instance of this event.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:SingleInstance"}, {"v": "scheduleFrequency:Weekly", "n": "Weekly", "d": "Schedule is on a weekly basis, typically occurring once per week.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleFrequency:Weekly"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ScheduleTiming', 'Types for when (in time) events occur.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ScheduleTiming', $j$[{"v": "scheduleTiming:Daytime", "n": "Daytime", "d": "Schedule is typically during daytime hours.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleTiming:Daytime"}, {"v": "scheduleTiming:Evening", "n": "Evening", "d": "Schedule is typically during evening hours.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleTiming:Evening"}, {"v": "scheduleTiming:Weekdays", "n": "Weekdays", "d": "Schedule is Monday through Friday, consecutively or non-consecutively.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleTiming:Weekdays"}, {"v": "scheduleTiming:Weekends", "n": "Weekends", "d": "Schedule is on a weekly basis, Saturday and/or Sunday.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: scheduleTiming:Weekends"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('ScoringMethod', 'Types of applicable scoring.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:ScoringMethod', $j$[{"v": "score:CriterionReferenced", "n": "Criterion-Referenced", "d": "Scored based on a comparison to defined criteria and levels of performance.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: score:CriterionReferenced"}, {"v": "score:NormReferenced", "n": "Norm-Referenced", "d": "Scored based on a comparison to a distribution of performance in a reference population.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: score:NormReferenced"}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('StatementCategory', 'Concepts used to classify the nature or purpose of structured statements.', 'If a more granular or precise classification is required for local purposes than is available in this concept scheme, best practice is to publish a description of it as a skos:Concept and to use it alongside the best match broader category in this scheme.', 'scheme: ceterms:StatementCategory', $j$[{"v": "statementCat:DevelopmentRelated", "n": "Development Related", "d": "Statement that defines commitments to joint development or future collaboration.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:DevelopmentRelated\ndct:description: May include curriculum alignment, program expansion, or new partnerships."}, {"v": "statementCat:EquivalencyRequestRelated", "n": "Equivalency Request Related", "d": "Statement that defines how a person requests determination of equivalency between an external academic resource and a receiving institution’s resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:EquivalencyRequestRelated\ndct:description: Covers process for course, credential, or program equivalency review."}, {"v": "statementCat:Guarantee", "n": "Guarantee", "d": "Statement that assures a condition, right, or outcome within the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:Guarantee\ndct:description: May include guarantees of credit acceptance, recognition, or services."}, {"v": "statementCat:LearningRecognitionEvidenceRelated", "n": "Learning Recognition Evidence Related", "d": "Statement that defines how evidence of prior learning evidence is accepted for evaluation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:LearningRecognitionEvidenceRelated"}, {"v": "statementCat:LearningRecognitionMethodRelated", "n": "Learning Recognition Method Related", "d": "Statement that defines the method(s) used to evaluate and recognize prior learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:LearningRecognitionMethodRelated"}, {"v": "statementCat:LearningRecognitionOutcomeRelated", "n": "Learning Recognition Outcome Related", "d": "Statement that defines the outcomes that are possible after evaluation of evidence of prior learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:LearningRecognitionOutcomeRelated"}, {"v": "statementCat:LearningRecognitionRequestRelated", "n": "Learning Recognition Request Related", "d": "Statement that defines how a person submits a request for recognition of prior learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:LearningRecognitionRequestRelated\ndct:description: Covers submission steps, forms or portals, timelines, fees, and evidence requirements."}, {"v": "statementCat:LearningRecognitionSourceRelated", "n": "Learning Recognition Source Related", "d": "Statement that defines the context from which prior learning may be recognized.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:LearningRecognitionSourceRelated"}, {"v": "statementCat:Limitation", "n": "Limitation", "d": "Statement that specifies a restriction or boundary on applicability.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:Limitation\ndct:description: Defines conditions under which transfer or recognition does not apply."}, {"v": "statementCat:MarketingRelated", "n": "Marketing Related", "d": "Statement that defines provisions for promoting the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:MarketingRelated\ndct:description: Covers branding, logos, co-marketing, and public announcements."}, {"v": "statementCat:MetricRelated", "n": "Metric Related", "d": "Statement that defines measures or performance indicators relevant to the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:MetricRelated\ndct:description: May include success rates, persistence, or evaluation metrics."}, {"v": "statementCat:MutualObligation", "n": "Mutual Obligation", "d": "Obligation that applies equally to all parties in the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:MutualObligation\nbroader: statementCat:Obligation\ndct:description: Often covers shared responsibilities such as maintaining accreditation."}, {"v": "statementCat:NoticePeriod", "n": "Notice Period", "d": "Statement that defines the time required for advance notice of actions such as termination or renewal.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:NoticePeriod\ndct:description: Often expressed in days, months, or academic terms."}, {"v": "statementCat:Obligation", "n": "Obligation", "d": "Statement that specifies a duty or responsibility under the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:Obligation\ndct:description: Parent concept for mutual, sender, and receiver obligations."}, {"v": "statementCat:Overview", "n": "Overview", "d": "Statement that summarizes the scope or general provisions of the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:Overview\ndct:description: Provides a high-level description without detailed terms."}, {"v": "statementCat:Purpose", "n": "Purpose", "d": "Statement that explains the intent or rationale of the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:Purpose\ndct:description: Clarifies why the agreement exists and what it seeks to achieve."}, {"v": "statementCat:ReceiverObligation", "n": "Receiver Obligation", "d": "Obligation that applies to the receiving party in the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:ReceiverObligation\nbroader: statementCat:Obligation\ndct:description: May include evaluating equivalency, applying transfer credit, or notifying learners."}, {"v": "statementCat:SenderObligation", "n": "Sender Obligation", "d": "Obligation that applies to the sending party in the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:SenderObligation\nbroader: statementCat:Obligation\ndct:description: May include providing transcripts, data, or verifying learning."}, {"v": "statementCat:TerminationTerms", "n": "Termination Terms", "d": "Statement that defines conditions for ending the agreement.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: statementCat:TerminationTerms\ndct:description: Includes triggers, procedures, and effective dates for termination."}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ctdl_tmp_valueset('SupportServiceCategory', 'Types of support services to help people succeed in their education and career goals.', NULL, 'scheme: ceterms:SupportServiceCategory', $j$[{"v": "support:AcademicAdvising", "n": "Academic Advising", "d": "Personalized process that assists people in achieving educational goals and navigating academic journeys.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:AcademicAdvising"}, {"v": "support:AssistiveTechnologySupport", "n": "Assistive Technology Support", "d": "Service that directly assists an individual in the selection, acquisition, or use of assistive technology devices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:AssistiveTechnologySupport"}, {"v": "support:AudiologicalHealthCare", "n": "Audiological Health Care", "d": "Health care and related services covering hearing loss or impairment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:AudiologicalHealthCare"}, {"v": "support:BehavioralService", "n": "Behavioral Service", "d": "Personalized service focused on addressing problem behaviors and developing positive and adaptive behaviors.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:BehavioralService"}, {"v": "support:BenefitsSupport", "n": "Benefits Support", "d": "Service that provides guidance and assistance to people in accessing and maintaining the financial and other benefits that can support their academic and career goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:BenefitsSupport\ndct:description: This can include support in understanding and maintaining eligibility, completing related forms, and navigating application and verification processes."}, {"v": "support:CareerAdvising", "n": "Career Advising", "d": "Personalized process that helps individuals identify and pursue their professional goals, and how to develop the skills and strategies necessary to achieve them.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CareerAdvising"}, {"v": "support:CareerAssessment", "n": "Career Assessment", "d": "Personalized process that helps individuals to identify their interests, skills, values, and personality traits, and to explore how they relate to different career paths and job opportunities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CareerAssessment"}, {"v": "support:CareerExploration", "n": "Career Exploration", "d": "Service that provides opportunities or information to discover and learn about careers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CareerExploration\ndct:description: This service can offer information and experiences about job market trends, salary expectations, working conditions and other factors that can help people identify and pursue their career goals."}, {"v": "support:CaseManagement", "n": "Case Management", "d": "Long-term, client-centered service for delivering comprehensive health and human services that involves ongoing assessment, planning, coordination, monitoring, and evaluation of a client's needs and services provided.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CaseManagement"}, {"v": "support:Chatbot", "n": "Chatbot", "d": "An interactive digital service that answers questions.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Chatbot\ndct:description: Format and technology neutral; may be embedded on web pages or portals, may be driven by AI or similar technology."}, {"v": "support:Childcare", "n": "Childcare", "d": "Provision of supervision, care, and activities for children in the absence of their parents or guardians.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Childcare"}, {"v": "support:ClothingAssistance", "n": "Clothing Assistance", "d": "Service that pays for or provides clothing to people who need appropriate attire.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:ClothingAssistance"}, {"v": "support:ComputerHub", "n": "Computer Hub", "d": "Physical location for accessing computers and other technology resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:ComputerHub"}, {"v": "support:Counseling", "n": "Counseling", "d": "Personalized process that helps individuals improve their mental health and well-being by exploring their emotions, behaviors, and relationships with the guidance of a trained professional.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Counseling\ndct:description: Personalized service that provides guidance and support to individuals experiencing personal, work-related, or academic challenges."}, {"v": "support:CreditTransferTool", "n": "Credit Transfer Tool", "d": "Online tool that estimates how previously earned credits or other types of prior learning transfers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CreditTransferTool"}, {"v": "support:CrisisSupport", "n": "Crisis Support", "d": "Services that provide immediate assistance to people who are facing unexpected challenges or crises that may interfere with their ability to pursue their academic or career goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:CrisisSupport\ndct:description: These services can include financial assistance, housing assistance, crisis hotlines, and counseling services among others."}, {"v": "support:DiversityEquityInclusion", "n": "Diversity Equity Inclusion", "d": "Services, programs, and initiatives that promote a welcoming and inclusive environment for individuals of all backgrounds.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:DiversityEquityInclusion"}, {"v": "support:EquipmentProvision", "n": "Equipment Provision", "d": "Service that provides people with access to the equipment, tools, or other physical resources necessary for education, training, or work.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:EquipmentProvision"}, {"v": "support:FinancialLiteracy", "n": "Financial Literacy", "d": "Provides people with the knowledge, skills, and resources necessary to make informed decisions about managing their personal finances.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:FinancialLiteracy"}, {"v": "support:FrequentlyAskedQuestions", "n": "Frequently Asked Questions", "d": "A curated support resource that provides answers to common questions.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:FrequentlyAskedQuestions\ndct:description: Format-neutral; may be web, print, or knowledge-base."}, {"v": "support:HealthCare", "n": "Health Care", "d": "Programs whose primary purpose is to help individuals achieve and maintain physical well-being through the study, prevention, screening, evaluation and treatment of individuals who have illnesses, injuries, or disabilities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:HealthCare"}, {"v": "support:ImmigrationAssistance", "n": "Immigration Assistance", "d": "Assistance for people in navigating legal and administrative procedures involved in immigrating to a new country.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:ImmigrationAssistance\ndct:description: Examples include assistance with visa applications, documentation requirements, and settlement services."}, {"v": "support:InternetAccess", "n": "Internet Access", "d": "Service where individuals can connect to the internet using their own devices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:InternetAccess"}, {"v": "support:JobPlacement", "n": "Job Placement", "d": "Assistance for individuals in finding suitable work.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:JobPlacement\ndct:description: Examples include providing job searching and matching resources, and facilitating the application, interview, and background check processes."}, {"v": "support:LearningResourceProvision", "n": "Learning Resource Provision", "d": "Service that provides people with access to educational materials.", "u": "Use for libraries and specialized resource centers.", "notes": "concept: support:LearningResourceProvision\ndct:description: Examples of support materials include textbooks, multimedia resources, research papers, journals, and online courses."}, {"v": "support:LegalService", "n": "Legal Service", "d": "Service that provides people with advice, representation, and/or support in navigating the legal system.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:LegalService\ndct:description: Examples include the interpretation and application of laws and regulations, and advocating for the individual's legal rights and interests."}, {"v": "support:MentalHealthCounseling", "n": "Mental Health Counseling", "d": "Personalized service that provides therapeutic support to individuals experiencing mental health issues such as anxiety, depression, or trauma.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:MentalHealthCounseling\ndct:description: Examples of mental health issues include behavior problems, emotional disturbances, personality disorders, incipient illnesses, and/or other comparable conditions."}, {"v": "support:Mentoring", "n": "Mentoring", "d": "Service that pairs individuals with people experienced in professions who can offer guidance and support as they pursue their academic or career goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Mentoring"}, {"v": "support:Networking", "n": "Networking", "d": "Service that connects people with employers and professional communities to expand their professional networks and gain access to new job opportunities and career pathways.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Networking\ndct:description: Examples include providing opportunities to attend networking events and connect with professionals."}, {"v": "support:NeurodivergenceService", "n": "Neurodivergence Service", "d": "Services related to neurodivergence.", "u": "Use for services relating to autism, tics/Tourettes Syndrome, Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD), and other similar conditions.", "notes": "concept: support:NeurodivergenceService\ndct:description: Neurodivergence means relating to having a mind that functions in ways that are not considered typical according to societal norms."}, {"v": "support:NoteTakingAssistance", "n": "Note Taking Assistance", "d": "Service that assists individuals to make their own record of classes or lectures.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:NoteTakingAssistance"}, {"v": "support:PeerService", "n": "Peer Service", "d": "Service that specializes in facilitating peer interaction.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PeerService\ndct:description: Examples include peer interactions such as counseling, tutoring, and leadership activities."}, {"v": "support:PersonalAssistance", "n": "Personal Assistance", "d": "Personalized service to help and accompany an individual who would otherwise be unable to participate in education, training, and/or work.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PersonalAssistance"}, {"v": "support:PortfolioAdvising", "n": "Portfolio Advising", "d": "A service that helps learners plan and prepare assessment-ready portfolios aligned to defined outcomes and institutional expectations.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PortfolioAdvising"}, {"v": "support:PostalAddress", "n": "Postal Address", "d": "Service to provide people who do not have a suitable mailing address with a means to receive their mail.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PostalAddress\ndct:description: This service is intended to help individuals receive documents and correspondence."}, {"v": "support:PriorLearningAssessmentAdvising", "n": "Prior Learning Assessment Advising", "d": "A service that guides learners in selecting, documenting, and submitting evidence for recognition of prior learning.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PriorLearningAssessmentAdvising"}, {"v": "support:PsychologicalService", "n": "Psychological Service", "d": "Personalized service that provides assessment, diagnosis, and treatment for mental health disorders.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PsychologicalService"}, {"v": "support:PublicBenefitsCaseManagement", "n": "Public Benefits Case Management", "d": "Specialized, long-term, and client-centered service for delivering comprehensive public benefits services that involves ongoing assessment, planning, coordination, monitoring, and evaluation of a client's needs and services provided related to public assistance programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:PublicBenefitsCaseManagement"}, {"v": "support:ReaderService", "n": "Reader Service", "d": "Service for reading text or describing visual content.", "u": "For pre-recorded formats such as audio books use the accommodationType property with the value \"AlternativeFormats\".", "notes": "concept: support:ReaderService"}, {"v": "support:Rehabilitation", "n": "Rehabilitation", "d": "Service that provides a combination of treatment and education designed to restore maximum functioning, independence,  and a sense of well-being for individuals who have temporary or permanent disabilities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Rehabilitation"}, {"v": "support:ResidentialLiving", "n": "Residential Living", "d": "Service that provides a therapeutic living environment in community-based residential facilities for individuals with special needs, including those with emotional and/or behavioral problems.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:ResidentialLiving"}, {"v": "support:RespiteCare", "n": "Respite Care", "d": "Service that provides temporary care to relieve a caregiver.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:RespiteCare"}, {"v": "support:SignLanguage", "n": "Sign Language", "d": "Service that provides sign language interpretation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:SignLanguage"}, {"v": "support:SkillMapping", "n": "Skill Mapping", "d": "Service that helps identify and assess an individual's specific skills and qualifications to determine any gaps or overlaps in their knowledge or experience as they relate to a career pathway.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:SkillMapping\ndct:description: This process can identify opportunities for advanced standing, transfer credit, or other forms of recognition for their skills, which can help people save time and money in pursuit of their education or career goals."}, {"v": "support:StudySkills", "n": "Study Skills", "d": "Service that provides assistance for people who want to improve their study habits, test preparation skills and test-taking techniques.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:StudySkills"}, {"v": "support:SubstanceAbusePrevention", "n": "Substance Abuse Prevention", "d": "Service related to preventing the misuse or abuse of drugs, alcohol, or other substances.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:SubstanceAbusePrevention"}, {"v": "support:SupportCoordination", "n": "Support Coordination", "d": "Service that involves coordinating and integrating various other services to provide comprehensive support to individuals.", "u": "Use for services known as \"wraparound services\" in the U.S.", "notes": "concept: support:SupportCoordination\ndct:description: Support coordination emphasizes a holistic and personalized approach where services are delivered in a comprehensive manner, rather than in isolation."}, {"v": "support:SupportedWork", "n": "Supported Work", "d": "Service that helps people with special needs find and retain paid work.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:SupportedWork\ndct:description: This can include advocacy and support services to address behaviors and basic skills required to stay employed."}, {"v": "support:TalentMarketplaceSignaling", "n": "Talent Marketplace Signaling", "d": "Service that enables employers to provide information that helps education and training providers align their offerings to current and future job opportunities.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TalentMarketplaceSignaling"}, {"v": "support:TechnologyLending", "n": "Technology Lending", "d": "Service that loans out technology equipment such as laptops, tablets, and other devices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TechnologyLending"}, {"v": "support:TestAssistance", "n": "Test Assistance", "d": "Service that provides assistance for people who need help in reading or writing responses to test items.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TestAssistance"}, {"v": "support:TransferAdmission", "n": "Transfer Admission", "d": "Service that provides information and support about the criteria and process for students applying as transfer candidates rather than first-time freshmen.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TransferAdmission"}, {"v": "support:TransferAdvising", "n": "Transfer Advising", "d": "A service that helps learners understand transfer options and applicability and plan efficient pathways to their goals.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TransferAdvising\ndct:description: Covers guidance on policies, prerequisites, timelines, and required documentation."}, {"v": "support:TransferEquivalencyTool", "n": "Transfer Equivalency Tool", "d": "Searchable system showing how courses from other institutions equate to local offerings.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TransferEquivalencyTool"}, {"v": "support:TransferOutreachEvent", "n": "Transfer Outreach Event", "d": "An event-based support service that informs and engages prospective transfer learners about pathways, policies, and resources.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TransferOutreachEvent\ndct:description: Includes fairs, info sessions, and campus visit programming."}, {"v": "support:TransferTimeline", "n": "Transfer Timeline", "d": "A support resource that outlines recommended steps and deadlines for completing transfer and recognition processes.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:TransferTimeline\ndct:description: Can be generalized or program-specific."}, {"v": "support:Translation", "n": "Translation", "d": "Service that provides spoken or written language translation.", "u": "For sign language, use Sign Language Service", "notes": "concept: support:Translation"}, {"v": "support:Transportation", "n": "Transportation", "d": "Service that provides or arranges  transportation for people.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:Transportation"}, {"v": "support:Tutoring", "n": "Tutoring", "d": "Individualized or small group teaching.", "u": "Tutoring as a support service is normally provided as a supplement to a regular teaching program.", "notes": "concept: support:Tutoring"}, {"v": "support:VisionService", "n": "Vision Service", "d": "Health care and related services related to vision loss or impairment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: support:VisionService"}]$j$::jsonb);

